      "snippet": {
        "text": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) has emerged as a transformative force in various industries, and its potential in the field of education is increasingly recognized. AI offers unique capabilities to enhance and revolutionize educational practices, addressing challenges, and unlocking new opportunities. This paper explores the role of AI in education, drawing insights from current research papers and highlighting its impact on teaching and learning. \n\nOne significant role of AI in education is its ability to facilitate personalized learning experiences. Li et al. (17) demonstrates how AI algorithms can analyze learner data, including performance, preferences, and behavior, to tailor educational content to individual needs. Personalized learning pathways help optimize engagement, knowledge retention, and skill development. Additionally, AI-powered adaptive learning systems, as studied by Khamparia et al. (18) , dynamically adjust content and difficulty levels based on real-time feedback, promoting self-paced and personalized learning experiences. \n\nAI plays a crucial role in transforming teaching and assessment practices. Kollöffel et al. (19) emphasizes the use of AI-based tutoring systems that provide real-time feedback, diagnose learning gaps, and offer targeted instructional support. These systems can analyze learner responses and adapt instructional strategies accordingly. Furthermore, AI-powered automated grading systems, as studied by Singh et al. (20) streamline the assessment process, providing faster and more consistent feedback, and allowing teachers to allocate more time to instructional activities. AI technologies enable the development of intelligent tutoring systems (ITS) and virtual assistants that support learners throughout their educational journey. \n\nVanlehn (21) highlights the capabilities of ITS to simulate human tutoring, adapt to individual needs, and provide personalized guidance. Virtual assistants, as studied by Yang et al. (22) use natural language processing and machine learning to respond to student queries, offer explanations, and provide guidance, fostering independent learning. AI-based educational analytics empower educators and administrators to make datadriven decisions. \n\nBaker (23) emphasizes the role of AI in analyzing educational data, such as learner performance, engagement, and demographic information, to identify patterns, predict outcomes, and inform instructional strategies. \n\nData-driven insights enable educators to customize interventions, identify at-risk students, and optimize educational resources.",
