        }
      },
      "snippet": {
        "text": "This study offers several important implications for practitioners and policymakers seeking to promote and facilitate the adoption of AI technologies in education. A supportive environment for AI integration must be established by school leaders and policymakers, with comprehensive strategies that emphasize the practical benefits of AI tools. These efforts should leverage credible channels such as Ministry of Education guidelines to ensure accurate and trustworthy communication. \n\nAllocating resources is an essential foundation for AI adoption, encompassing investments in infrastructure, tools, and technical support to remove barriers and ensure equitable access across schools. For instance, hands-on workshops, where teachers can interact with AI tools like ChatGPT or Canva, are particularly effective in building confidence and illustrating practical applications such as content creation (e.g., creating lesson plans), administrative tasks (e.g., automating grading) and personalized learning. \n\nProviding targeted information about AI through workshops, online materials, and collaborative learning communities is equally critical. Collaborative cohorts where teachers co-design AI-enhanced lesson plans foster a sense of community and shared learning. Peer-shared success stories and case studies can further demonstrate AI's real-world benefits, inspiring broader adoption by showcasing its impact on tasks like simplifying administration and enhancing student engagement. \n\nTailored training programs are vital for building teachers' self-efficacy and intrinsic motivation. These programs should focus on practical, real-world applications of AI, transparency in how AI tools function, and addressing privacy concerns to build trust. Exposing teachers to accurate information about AI through trusted channels-such as ministry guidelines, peer case studies, and professional communities-reduces misconceptions and fosters positive attitudes toward the usefulness and ease of use of AI tools. \n\nPolicymakers should prioritize the development of comprehensive strategies that allocate resources for infrastructure, technical support, and professional development. Recognition programs or rewards for innovative AI implementation can further nurture a culture of exploration and continuous learning. \n\nAdditionally, approaches should be tailored to the diverse needs of teachers. For intrinsically motivated teachers, autonomy and flexibility are essential to encourage innovation and creativity. Strengthening internal motivations through positive evaluations and meaningful incentives can foster a culture of experimentation. For teachers who rely on institutional guidelines, clear and transparent directives from education ministries, coupled with training programs aligned with individual teaching styles, can enhance self-efficacy and motivation, facilitating seamless AI integration.",
