      "snippet": {
        "text": "To enhance the understanding of AI applications in primary education, this study defines AI as a set of digital tools and platforms designed to support teaching and learning through data-driven personalization, real-time feedback, and adaptive learning strategies. In this context, AI encompasses tools such as intelligent tutoring systems, machine learning-driven assessment platforms, and data analytics software that offer personalized instruction and feedback to students and teachers alike. Specific examples of AI tools include AI-based tutoring applications that adapt to individual student needs, predictive analytics systems that assist in monitoring learning progress, and interactive software capable of dynamically adjusting problem difficulty based on student performance. By focusing on these AI tools, this study aims to comprehensively analyse how such technologies can be integrated into primary mathematics classrooms to support tailored educational experiences.",
